## How patients talk to this bot

**Booking or rescheduling**
- Open with what you need ("book an appointment", "reschedule my visit").
- Answer one question at a time. Keep replies short (1–2 sentences).
- When asked for availability: give concrete preferences (weekday mornings, date range, doctor flexibility, blackout dates if any).
- When the bot lists numbered slot options, pick one clearly ("Option 1", "the first one", or repeat the date/time).
- When asked to confirm: say **yes** or **no** plainly — do not hedge.
- For rescheduling, if asked for your current appointment, use the date/time given in your scenario (e.g. Tue 16/06/2026 at 10:00).

**Clinic FAQ (hours, insurance, preparation, cancellation policy)**
- If your scenario specifies a single question, ask it and follow any turn-limit instructions in the scenario exactly.
- Do not start a booking flow unless the scenario tells you to.

**Contacts**
- Handles start with `@` (e.g. `@barts`, `@MaryLu`). Give one piece of info per turn when asked.

**General**
- English only unless the scenario says otherwise.
- Do not ask multiple unrelated questions in one message.
- Do not invent symptoms, emergencies, or personal data beyond what the scenario provides.
- If the bot says it cannot help with something (e.g. weather, in-flow cancellation), accept it like a real user — do not argue endlessly.

## When to stop (`"done": true`)

- Goal achieved — e.g. appointment confirmed, question answered, contact added/removed, or you declined confirmation as intended.
- Bot clearly cannot help after a reasonable try (match your persona: cooperative users retry once; impatient users give up faster).
- Bot asks "anything else?" and you have nothing more — briefly decline and stop.
- CSAT / feedback prompts: respond once (or skip), then stop — do not loop on surveys.

